language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Ship each product from origins to destinations at minimum total cost, within origin supplies, destination demands and origin-destination limits.
given supply_dim1, supply_dim2 : int(1..)
given supply : matrix indexed by [int(1..supply_dim1), int(1..supply_dim2)] of int(0..)
given demand_dim1 : int(1..)
given demand : matrix indexed by [int(1..demand_dim1), int(1..supply_dim2)] of int(0..)
given limit : matrix indexed by [int(1..supply_dim1), int(1..demand_dim1)] of int(0..)
given cost_dim1, cost_dim2, cost_dim3 : int(1..)
given cost : matrix indexed by [int(1..cost_dim1), int(1..cost_dim2), int(1..cost_dim3)] of int(0..)
find ship : matrix indexed by [int(1..supply_dim1), int(1..demand_dim1), int(1..supply_dim2)] of int(0..100000)
find total_cost : int(0..10000000)

branching on [ship]

minimising total_cost
such that
$ the total cost is the sum over origins, destinations and products of the unit cost times the amount shipped
total_cost = (sum i : int(1..supply_dim1) . (sum j : int(1..demand_dim1) . (sum p : int(1..supply_dim2) . cost[i,j,p] * ship[i,j,p]))),
$ the amount of each product shipped out of an origin does not exceed its supply
forAll i : int(1..supply_dim1) . forAll p : int(1..supply_dim2) . ((sum j : int(1..demand_dim1) . ship[i,j,p]) <= supply[i,p]),
$ the amount of each product shipped into a destination meets its demand exactly (shipping more never lowers cost, so the demand is met with equality)
forAll j : int(1..demand_dim1) . forAll p : int(1..supply_dim2) . ((sum i : int(1..supply_dim1) . ship[i,j,p]) = demand[j,p]),
$ the total shipped from an origin to a destination, over all products, does not exceed their limit
forAll i : int(1..supply_dim1) . forAll j : int(1..demand_dim1) . ((sum p : int(1..supply_dim2) . ship[i,j,p]) <= limit[i,j]),
$ a shipment of one product from an origin to a destination never exceeds the supply of that product at the origin (implied by the supply rule)
forAll i : int(1..supply_dim1) . forAll j : int(1..demand_dim1) . forAll p : int(1..supply_dim2) . (ship[i,j,p] <= supply[i,p]),
$ a shipment of one product from an origin to a destination never exceeds the demand of that product at the destination (implied, costs are non-negative)
forAll i : int(1..supply_dim1) . forAll j : int(1..demand_dim1) . forAll p : int(1..supply_dim2) . (ship[i,j,p] <= demand[j,p])
